Database migrations for nj-cli (SQLite via SQLAlchemy).

CONNECTION
    The URL is not in alembic.ini. env.py builds it from the environment:
        NJ_ALEMBIC_URL   full URL, wins when set (use for scratch databases)
        NJ_DB_PATH       path only, defaults to data/nj.db

COMMON COMMANDS
    poetry run alembic upgrade head        apply everything outstanding
    poetry run alembic current             what this database is at
    poetry run alembic check               is the ORM ahead of the migrations?
    poetry run alembic downgrade -1        roll back one revision

ADDING A MIGRATION
    1. Change nj/db/models.py.
    2. poetry run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    3. poetry run ruff format alembic/      (alembic's generated body is not
       ruff-format clean; the template header already is)
    4. Read the generated file. Autogenerate does not detect renames — it emits
       a drop plus an add, which loses the column's data. Rewrite those by hand.
    5. poetry run pytest tests/unit/test_migrations.py

    tests/unit/test_migrations.py fails if you skip step 2, so drift cannot
    reach main unnoticed.

AN EXISTING DATABASE
    Databases created before Alembic was introduced already have their tables,
    so `upgrade head` would fail trying to create them again. Mark such a
    database as current instead, once:

        poetry run alembic stamp head

    data/nj.db was stamped at the baseline revision on 2026-08-17.

SQLITE
    SQLite cannot ALTER a column, so env.py sets render_as_batch=True and
    Alembic rebuilds the table instead. This is already configured; you do not
    need to do anything for it, but it is why generated migrations that touch
    columns are wrapped in batch_alter_table blocks.
